<title>UK: GEC mum on Thompson-CSF bid reports.</title>
<headline>GEC mum on Thompson-CSF bid reports.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's GEC Plc had no immediate comment on Wednesday on French newspaper reports that it had declared itself a candidate for the acquisition of the French state's 58-percent stake in defence electronics group Thomson-CSF.</p>
<p>A GEC spokesman said the company had not prepared a statement on the subject and could not comment further.</p>
<p>Earlier, French daily newspapers said GEC's bid rivalled two other bids by Lagardere Groupe and Alcatel Alsthom.</p>
<p>La Tribune newspaper said that the government would decide on Friday which of the bids were valid and would be taken into further consideration.</p>
<p>--London newsroom, +44 171 542 7717</p>
